`neutron dev` runs this project's `neutron-ts dev` (Vite), passing
`NEUTRON_PORT` / `NEUTRON_HOST` as `--port` / `--host` when they are set
(default port {{.Port}}). `npm run dev` does the same without that translation.

| Command | Action |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run build` | Production build into `dist/` |
| `npm start -- --port 3000` | Serve the production build |
| `npm run typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |

## Routes

- `src/routes/index.tsx` → `/`; add a page by adding a file under `src/routes/`
- `src/routes/_layout.tsx` wraps every page
- `src/main.tsx` is framework glue — do not edit it (see `AGENTS.md`)

`GET /health` (`{"status", "nucleus", "version"}`) is built into the
production server (`npm start`). The Vite dev server does not serve it.

## Configuration

`NEUTRON_DATABASE_URL` in `.env` is for your own loaders and actions; the
framework does not read it. Nothing loads `.env` automatically.

Docs: https://neutron.build/docs
